**Reasoning:**
- Refining each candidate (rather than only the best greedy result) lets the hill-climb explore multiple local optima; the best-of-6 refined placements is guaranteed no worse than before and often better on tight instances.
- Swap moves matter when memory is nearly saturated: a plain move may not fit anywhere, but exchanging a large low-pressure model for a small high-pressure model between GPUs can rebalance pressure without violating memory limits. The swap feasibility check `m2.model_size <= m.model_size + dst_free` is exact.
- Complexity remains small (6 greedy runs + bounded hill-climb), so execution time stays well under the limit.
